Context
  Asked for a setup portion so Guile projects look similar -- core Makefile, src
  layout, tests, then Emacs support -- and to do it in a separate tree because the
  work is extensive. Then asked to look in ../guile-* or fetch a real application
  such as rekado/guile-irc.

  This is a sibling worktree per the house convention:
  ghq/github.com/dsp-dr/guile-skills-scaffold on feat/guile-project-scaffold.

Deviations
  Surveyed first, built second. The request implied a standard shape; the corpus
  says there is no single shape to standardize on -- src/ is 43% -- so the first
  artifact is a detector rather than a template. Templates that assume src/ would
  have been wrong for the majority of the projects they were meant to serve.

  guile-irc was cloned with ghq get as asked, and read only as reference. Nothing
  from it is vendored.

Considerations
  Deliberately non-deployable: the detector is in scripts/, not scripts/lib/, so
  nothing ships and no version moves. check-version-bump.sh caught the first
  placement, which is the gate working as designed rather than an obstacle.

  The survey is reproducible but its script lives in the session scratchpad, not
  the repo. If the corpus matrix (roadmap D7) gets built, that script is the
  starting point and belongs in tests/ with the numbers committed.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, as dsp-dr. 48 projects
  surveyed, 12 used for calibration. gmake checks green.
